{
  "_doc": "Base fauna (25 species, ROADMAP \u00a74.1). Palettes drive part rendering via @primary/@secondary/@accent tokens. tags feed the battle chart; class is the species' natural elemental class (a chimera's actual class is derived from its parts' classAffinity \u2014 see data/classes.json); archetype selects the shape family used by tools/gen-parts.js. Ranch fields: frame = torso for a purebred; diet/feedCost = one feed action; upkeepPerDay = housing drain; mailOrderPrice = catalog price (null = not sold, acquired by conquering region nodes that unlock its fauna); growthHours = age-stage thresholds; thermal = [minC,maxC] comfort band, intersected across a chimera's species; setBonus = purebred bonus at 4+ parts; incubationMinutes = egg timer. VARIANTS (post-v0.1, ROADMAP \u00a73.2): a species with `variantOf` is the same stock, mutated \u2014 it inherits its base's anatomy and frame, and carries its own palette, tags, thermal band, set bonus and `statMult`. Never strictly better: every variant trades something, or the base species becomes dead content the moment you breed one. `affinity` overrides a slot's classAffinity (a Glider Skunk's forelimbs vote Air), and `shapeTweak` nudges the generator's shape params so a variant is not merely a recolour. mailOrderPrice is null on all of them \u2014 variants are bred, never bought. `moveTag` appends a tag to a variant's damaging MOVES, which is where the tag chart actually reads \u2014 a variant whose identity only shows up on the defending side is a dead mechanic.",
